course: dictionary
lesson: 5888
title: Finding a word's meaning in a story
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A story often shows you what a word means. «The photo ended up on Gran's mantelpiece, and every time Maddie saw it she remembered that the shove came first.» Photos are put on a mantelpiece so people can see them, so a mantelpiece must be a place in a room where things are kept on display.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the new word. «Picture Charlie's great-grandmother at her 100th birthday, a card from the King on the mantelpiece» tells you a card was set out on it, in the room where the birthday was. Ask yourself: where would you put a card so that everyone could see it?
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A mantelpiece can be the shelf above a fireplace, or the frame around a fireplace. Read the whole sentence to decide which meaning fits. If you are still not sure, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: A mantelpiece is the shelf above a fireplace.
fact: The word can also mean the frame around a fireplace.
fact: People often put clocks, cards, ornaments or photos on a mantelpiece.
fact: Mantel and mantelshelf are other words for it.
fact: In detective stories, a clue is often found «on the mantelpiece».
exercise: «The photo ended up on Gran's mantelpiece.» Where was the photo? | Under the bed | In the garden shed | *On the shelf above the fireplace | In the kitchen sink
exercise: A mantelpiece is which of these? | A window in a bedroom | A plate for dinner | *A shelf above a fireplace | A kind of hat worn at parties
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that tells you where the card was kept. «Picture Charlie's great-grandmother at her 100th birthday, a card from the King on the mantelpiece» | a card from the King | great-grandmother | at her 100th birthday | *on the mantelpiece
test: In a detective story, where might a clue be found? | In the garden shed | In the school bag | Under the sea | *On the mantelpiece
test: Which word means the same as mantelpiece? | Doorstep | Window | *Mantelshelf | Carpet
exam: Which best describes a mantelpiece? | A long road by the sea | A bed for the dog | *A shelf above a fireplace, where ornaments or cards may stand | A type of cake
